---
const navItems = [
  // D100's shape B was MEASURED on this label set — three links plus the mark (see the probe output
  // in .design/grill/navfit/). Adding "Home" back makes the row need 313px in the narrow tier and
  // 376px in the wide tier, which overflows a 320 viewport's 288 by 25 and a 390's 342 by 34; the
  // nav is nowrap on purpose, so that shows up as a failed probe, not a re-wrap. The mark is the
  // home path (href "/", aria-label names the club), which is why a fourth link is redundant as well
  // as expensive.
  { href: '/schedule', label: 'Schedule' },
  { href: '/chat', label: 'Chat' },
  { href: '/members', label: 'Members' }
];
---

<header class="bg-paper">
  <nav class="max-w-screen-xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-4">
    <!-- D100 shape B, measured in .design/grill/nav-fit.html: one row at every width, the mark
         shortened to "MPLS Math Club" so the row needs 310px and a 375 viewport's content box is
         343. Below the `nav-narrow` breakpoint (360px) the links take the already-ratified 11.1px
         chrome step and the gap goes to 8px: needs 262px, fits a 320's 288 and a 300's 268.

         `flex-nowrap` is the load-bearing part. The shipped nav was `flex-col` + `flex-wrap`, which
         is why the page clipped and links disappeared (A needed 397px, more than every content box
         this site ships). With nowrap, a future label set that stops fitting shows up as a failed
         width probe in `npm run check:render` instead of a silent re-wrap. -->
    <div class="flex flex-nowrap items-center gap-2 nav-narrow:gap-4">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="flex-shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap py-2 font-body text-body text-ink"
        aria-label="Minneapolis Math Book Club, home"
      >
        MPLS <em class="not-italic text-gold">Math</em> Club
      </a>
      <div class="flex flex-nowrap items-center gap-2 nav-narrow:gap-4">
        {navItems.map(item => (
          <a
            href={item.href}
            class="whitespace-nowrap py-2 text-micro nav-narrow:text-label text-ink font-medium hover:text-gold"
            aria-label={`Navigate to ${item.label}`}
          >
            {item.label}
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>
</header>
